  <dashboards>
    <dashboard name="Title">
      <style />
      <size maxheight='760' maxwidth='1100' minheight='760' minwidth='1100' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <datasources />
      <zones>
        <zone h='760' id='101' type-v2='layout-basic' w='1100' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='680' id='102' type-v2='text' w='980' x='60' y='40'>
            <formatted-text><run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='26'>Retail REITs: Who Is Winning, and Does It Show Up in the Stock?</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='15'>ISA 401 Final Project  |  Fall 2026  |  Section A  |  Team [#]</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='15'>Tyler Draeger  &amp;  Kenneth Kelly</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='16'>The question</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>Among the 24 publicly traded U.S. retail REITs, are shopping center owners doing better than malls and net-lease REITs on occupancy and rent growth, and does that show up in stock returns and valuations, or do interest rates matter more?</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='16'>Where the data comes from</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='13'>- Nareit REIT directory (web scraping): the list of retail REITs, returns, dividend yields, headquarters</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='13'>- SEC EDGAR (API): revenue, net income, assets, and liabilities every quarter</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='13'>- 370 quarterly earnings press releases (LLM extraction): occupancy, same-property NOI growth, FFO</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='13'>- FRED (API): 10-year Treasury yield   |   Yahoo Finance (API): daily stock prices</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#666666' fontsize='12'>Use the Property Type filter on each page to focus on one group. Hover over any mark for details.</run></formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{383E61EC-0133-4E5C-A5EC-656AD2EFEA20}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name="Takeaways">
      <style />
      <size maxheight='760' maxwidth='1100' minheight='760' minwidth='1100' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <datasources />
      <zones>
        <zone h='760' id='103' type-v2='layout-basic' w='1100' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='680' id='104' type-v2='text' w='980' x='60' y='40'>
            <formatted-text><run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f3b57' fontsize='24'>Takeaways</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>1.  Shopping centers have the strongest fundamentals: occupancy keeps rising and same-property NOI grows about 4% a year, faster than malls.</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>2.  Malls are the cheapest and most indebted group, and the stocks bounced the most as investors came back to them.</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>3.  Net-lease REITs are almost 100% leased but behave like bonds: their returns move the most with the 10-year Treasury.</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='14'>4.  Interest rates still drive a lot of the quarter-to-quarter stock moves for every group, so strong property results do not always show up in the stock right away.</run><run>&#10;</run><run>&#10;</run><run fontcolor='#666666' fontsize='12'>Limits: 2023-2026 only; FFO and occupancy come from company press releases (checked against the text); a few of the newest quarters are not in the SEC data yet.</run></formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='12' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{BFA927C6-1168-4BBC-97EA-CD38E501B5C4}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name='Retail REIT Story' type='storyboard'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='900' maxwidth='1100' minheight='900' minwidth='1100' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <datasources />
      <zones>
        <zone h='900' id='107' type-v2='layout-basic' w='1100' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='900' id='108' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='1100' x='0' y='0'>
            <zone h='36' id='109' type-v2='title' w='1100' x='0' y='0' />
            <zone h='90' id='105' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='106' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='1100' x='0' y='36' />
            <zone h='774' id='106' paired-zone-id='105' type-v2='flipboard' w='1100' x='0' y='126'>
              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                <story-point captured-sheet="Title" caption="Retail REITs: the question" id='1' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="Occupancy Trend" caption="Occupancy: net lease is full, centers are catching up" id='2' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="NOI Growth Trend" caption="Growth: shopping centers lead" id='3' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="Valuation vs Growth" caption="Is growth rewarded?" id='4' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="Returns vs Rates" caption="Interest rates move the stocks" id='5' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="1-Year Return by REIT" caption="Last year's winners" id='6' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="Debt Load by REIT" caption="Who carries the most debt" id='7' />
                <story-point captured-sheet="Takeaways" caption="Takeaways" id='8' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{6348E9FF-6F8B-401C-8EFC-7F541E07DEF2}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
